  },
  {
   "t": "11. PYELONEPHRITIS → ADMIT: ceftriaxone 1 g IV daily (or gentamicin 6 mg/kg IV daily) + NaCl 0.9% up to 3 L/24 h. SEPTIC SHOCK → resuscitate, REFER — Pyelonephritis: start antibiotics promptly†, then continue on the UTI management chart and the 24-hour nursing record.",
   "s": "adultstg2026:6.32"
  }
 ],
